body: "## Hosted failure on the current PR head\nAt `ef654dd14c7753e5be31a4edc6fda684cf7c8edc` (PR #196), [Node 22 job 123249088559](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40813502905/job/123249088559) passes the npm full release gate but fails the Bun full release gate: **440 tests pass, 1 fails**.\n\nThe failing test is [test/zero-budget.test.ts:57](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/ef654dd14c7753e5be31a4edc6fda684cf7c8edc/test/zero-budget.test.ts#L57), “exact 512-byte receipt succeeds through installed Node and Bun CLI without Git”. The decoded job log at 03:52:27 UTC reports:\n```\nError: ENOTEMPTY: directory not empty, rmdir '<temporary-zero-budget-fixture>/.bun/install/cache/@t@'\n    at Object.rmdirSync (node:fs:1193:11)\n    at _rmdirSync (node:internal/fs/rimraf:261:21)\n```\nThe test registers recursive synchronous fixture removal in its after hook. This is a hosted teardown failure, not a demonstrated production selector failure. The temporary fixture name above is normalized.\n\n## Expected / actual and impact\nExpected: the installed-CLI exact-ceiling regression finishes with reliable cleanup and no residual fixture activity.\nActual: cleanup fails in the Bun cache subtree, making the required Node 22 full gate red despite the npm gate passing. Node 26 npm and Bun gates pass on the same head. A prior code-head four-gate pass does not establish a final-head pass.\n\nIndependent bounded compiled-module checks at the same head pass 462 broad assertions plus 701 boundary assertions; all 200 exact-budget cases fail at the old head as a negative control. Those checks do **not** exercise native CLI/cache cleanup and do not override this failure.\n\n## Classification and limits\n**Observed hosted test failure; not locally reproduced.** A child/cache-lifecycle race is a hypothesis, not a verified root cause. This differs from the already-recorded suggested-command child timeout/null-exit in the PR body. No test thresholds, implementation, dependency pins or workflow retries were changed by this review.\n\nDedup checked all 196 all-status issue/PR records (two pages), latest PR body/discussion, and the [canonical shared-fragment feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/ef654dd14c7753e5be31a4edc6fda684cf7c8edc/.agents/pm/features/pm-context-shared-fragment-evidence.toon). No matching cleanup owner/acknowledgment was found. Existing Daily Release issues concern other runs and are not established owners of this new test failure.\n\n## Acceptance / regression protection\n- Establish which process/cache activity persists at fixture removal; await or explicitly close owned work rather than masking live background activity.\n- Make fixture cleanup reliable, with bounded retry only where appropriate after owned work has terminated.\n- Preserve the installed Node/Bun **exact 512-byte** assertions, non-Git coverage, source/compiled boundary properties and existing coverage thresholds.\n- Exercise the cleanup-sensitive regression repeatedly and obtain fresh full npm/Bun gates on Node 22 and Node 26 for the final head.\n- Keep the failed receipt and distinguish scoped regression success from full-gate success.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (3)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-29T04:18:59Z)\n>\n> ## Follow-through: bounded retry change still fails on the new head\n> \n> Verified at `09b6b967d46b549c8755c8d4b7d8f94ca9bbd749` in [Node 22 job 123254772647](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40815280262/job/123254772647). This head changes all four owned Bun fixture removals to `rmSync(..., { recursive: true, force: true, maxRetries: 10, retryDelay: 100 })`; product assertions/timeouts and runtime source are unchanged.\n> \n> The new Node 22 Bun gate still reports **441 tests, 440 pass, 1 fail, zero skipped**. At 04:11:34 UTC its failed-test section again identifies `test/zero-budget.test.ts:57`, the installed Node/Bun exact-512-byte test, with `ENOTEMPTY` in `<temporary-zero-budget-fixture>/.bun/install/cache/@t@` and `rmdirSync` / internal rimraf stack. The exact-boundary producer test passes immediately before it. Native source coverage reports 100% in all dimensions; this is not a coverage-percentage regression. Node 26's exact-head job is successful.\n> \n> **Conclusion:** the retry-only mitigation is present in source but does not establish cleanup recovery. Retain this issue as unresolved. The earlier receipt is not the sole remaining red run; this is a fresh failure after the change.\n> \n> **Limits:** hosted evidence, not an independent local reproduction. Background cache activity remains a hypothesis; the log alone does not identify the writer or prove why retries exhaust. No production packet/selector defect is established.\n> \n> Acceptance remains the existing lifecycle/cleanup investigation, bounded termination preserving hard failure, repeated cleanup-sensitive regression plus fresh full npm/Bun Node 22/26 gates at the final head, with all exact-budget assertions and thresholds retained. Verified canonical source: [shared-fragment feature at this head](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/09b6b967d46b549c8755c8d4b7d8f94ca9bbd749/.agents/pm/features/pm-context-shared-fragment-evidence.toon).\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-29T05:24:56Z)\n>\n> ## Follow-through: asynchronous cleanup passes fresh final-head gates\n> \n> At `d63ac9f1d4e8e4d80db636e0e224f059ebeacfa3`, the four owned fixture teardown sites now await a shared `fs/promises.rm` helper with bounded retries. The added `test/bun-fixture.test.ts` injects a real late write after directory enumeration. Runtime packet source, exact-budget assertions and dependency pins are unchanged.\n> \n> Verified decoded logs for [Node 22 job 123263505632](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40817983871/job/123263505632) and [Node 26 job 123263505887](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40817983871/job/123263505887): both npm and Bun complete gates report **442/442 tests passing, zero failures/skips** on both Node versions. This supersedes the failed retry-only head recorded above; keep that historical receipt rather than overwriting it.\n> \n> Independent isolated execution of the exact added cleanup test passes 1/1 on Node24.22.1. A local synchronous-adapter control did not trigger the intended injection on Node24, so it is **not** counted as an independent reproduction of the former Node22 failure. The actual old failure and new successful Node22 gates remain the evidence for that runtime.\n> \n> This is verified source/hosted regression recovery for the reported fixture-cleanup gate, not proof of the precise historical background writer, indefinite flake absence, whole-release certification, npm publication or deployment. No issue status changed by this review.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-02T09:26:31Z)\n>\n> Fixed on main. Evidence: PR #196 merged 2026-10-29T06:38Z (final head d63ac9f: shared async fs/promises.rm teardown with bounded retries); green 442/442 npm+Bun gates run 40817983871 (jobs 123263505632/123263505887); main CI success 41307066368 (Found in the 2026-11-02 triage of issues the blind issue watch missed.)"
